				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/abettik" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1700758); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1700758&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606250298" alt="Abettik" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1700758)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/abettik" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1700758); return false;" >Abettik</a></span> <span class="odate time_1519849622 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Feb 2018 20:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3724938">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>Hesitant upvote. I feel like there's a lot more potential here that you didn't capitalize on, but maybe that's my Next Generation fanboy just wanting more. So I guess for the most part, it's short, sweet, and imaginative.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Nitpicks, questions, suggestions:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Blasts of light have also been observed originating from SCP-3135-1, along with the launching of several torpedoes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Torpedoes&quot; is the Star Trek word for them, but I'm not sure the SCP foundation would call them such. The foundation might just call them projectiles, especially in a technical document like this. Same reason you have them refer to &quot;phasers&quot; as &quot;blasts of light.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These organisms appear to behave consistently with the portrayal of the Enterprise's crew in the original series&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Because <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Trek:_The_Original_Series">The Original Series</a> is essentially a Star Trek proper noun for the 1966 series, you should consider removing the word &quot;original&quot; or changing it to &quot;The Next Generation&quot; or &quot;the original run of the series.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There is a drastic increase in nudity, graphic violence, and profanity. The majority of said profanity can be attributed to the character of Data, who uses the word 'fuck' a minimum of ten times per episode.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's the reason for this? The fan author is trying to make it &quot;edgy?&quot; Why Data, the unfeeling android?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The character Jean Luc Picard's name is now John Luke Picard.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's the reason for this? An error on the fanboy's part? I feel like all trekkies can spell Jean-Luc Picard's name. If you're trying to show that the fanboy writing this can't spell someone's name, I would make it something -slightly- less well known. (Maybe Deanna Troi is Deanna Troy?)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The majority of episodes are now based around the character William Riker and his various sexual encounters.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I like this, because you're really getting at the crux of the concept here, which is that this is a fan work. You might add another bullet about how there are a lot more action scenes than in the original series, and that one character (Riker? Picard?) is constantly portrayed as a hero for his bravery and fighting ability or something.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks for writing this, and I look forward to reading more.</p>

							</div>

								
					
